<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n107383" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπερδεής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>, 
			Ep.
		 acc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπερδέᾰ,</span> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπερδεέα</span>: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέος</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>above all fear, undaunted,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπερδέα δῆμον ἔχοντας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					17.330
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
			</span></i> ad loc.; but <i><span class="en">
				Apollon.
				<u>Lex.</u>
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, derive it from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέομαι</span> (to
			want), <i>much less, inferior</i>: neither expl. is satisfactory
			and Brocks' cj. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὲρ Δία</span> should
			perh. be accepted.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
